Z||000000||kevin||03-15-2000||01:06 AM||||Suppose your Fiero with the '85 Duke had a little, but not so much power until the tach was @ 3,000 rpm. Suppose you checked the fuel filter, had new plugs, wires, rotor, 02 sensor and new IAC valve! You frequent visitors might remember I had a slow acceleration problem that half-way fixed itself last week. Recording the nature of this perplexing dilema, the slow acceleration happens most frequently when it is warm. I also noticed the exhaust header turns beat red-hot after 10 to 20 miles on the freeway. Can any Fiero lovers offer suggestions? I suppose you can....   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||03-15-2000||01:30 AM||||Sounds like a clogged catalytic converter to me.  Gentlemen?||||reg||1
Z||000002||b_b_a_d||03-15-2000||01:49 AM||||Suggestions...<P>Please don't drive it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  <P>You will surely burn up the valves if if is glowing beat red!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>A vacuum leak can cause the glowing exhaust manifold condition but I have to agree with shiner on this one.  The cat can cause similar conditions both glowing manifold from back pressure and lack of performance with acceleration.  <P>The only thing I am baffled by is the change in performance due to temperature.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||03-15-2000||08:57 AM||||If its not the Cat, then I would check the Muffler Bearings.....<P>Seriously, If you know that the timing is set right then I would say that the Cat is the problem.  It would probably only cost $20-30 to have a muffler shop cut it off and replace it with a straight pipe.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||03-15-2000||01:58 PM||||All good suggestions. The red manifold in combination with little power <B>below</B> 3000 would make me think timing (not enough advance). A bad cat. is more likely to cause more problem at <B>higher</B> RPM.<P>The order I would check:<BR>1. Timing<BR>2. Vacuum leak<BR>3. Cat.<P>BTW... if you forget to ground the diagnostic terminal while setting the timing the car will exhibit these sypmtoms. I refuse to say <B>how</B> I know this...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||03-15-2000||03:27 PM||||I agree. Vacuum leak, timing, then maybe cat. It should get worse at hight RPM if the cat was clogged.<P>I'll bet it's really lean. Could be a vacuum leak or the O2 is telling the ECM it's rich so the ECM is leaning it out. At 3000 RPM, it probably going into WOT/PE and the O2 is not used.<P>Have you changed the O2 lately? Have you used leaded gas lately?<P>Terry||||reg||1
